# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
# |<----  Max 50 Characters  ---->|
#
# Body: flat bulleted list, no indented sub-bullets (hard-wrap at 72 cols)
# - Explain why this change is needed
# - What was done (not how)
# - Any side effects to be aware of
#
# Footer (optional):
#   Fixes #issue
#   Closes #issue
#   BREAKING CHANGE: description
#
# --- COMMIT END ---
# Breaking change? Add ! after type/scope:  feat!: | fix(scope)!:
#
# Types:
#   feat     (new feature — MINOR bump)
#   fix      (bug fix — PATCH bump)
#   docs     (documentation only)
#   style    (formatting, no logic change)
#   refactor (code restructuring)
#   perf     (performance improvement — PATCH bump)
#   test     (adding/updating tests)
#   build    (build system / dependencies)
#   ci       (CI configuration)
#   chore    (maintenance, tooling)
#   revert   (reverting changes)
#
# Scopes (examples):
#   renderer, audio, ai, map, hud, water, terrain, model,
#   menu, network, build, deps, game, controls
#
# Subject: imperative mood, present tense, no period
#   ✅ "fix: prevent null pointer in user lookup"
#   ❌ "fixed null pointer bug"
#   ❌ "Fix: null pointer bug."
#
# Remember: one logical change per commit
